dsh-artifacts
=============

This package is an independent, from-scratch implementation of three public
protocol ideas, with new code throughout. No source files from the projects
below are copied or vendored; their contracts were read to make the merged
surface compatible, and their licenses are reproduced here for attribution.

1. dsh-genui — MIT
   Repository: https://github.com/omdsh-dev/dsh-genui
   Package:    @changfenhuang/dsh-genui
   Contributed: the declarative `spec` channel (a JSON component tree rendered
   inline), its action-event loop back to the model, and its bundled-skill
   posture.

2. dsh-visualize — BSD-3-Clause
   Repository: https://github.com/Nagi-ovo/dsh-visualize
   Contributed: the sandboxed inline-HTML card (fragment wrapped in a frame
   with its own CSP), the streaming/partial-render posture, and the
   `inline | wide | page` surface modes.

3. dsh-generative-ui — Apache-2.0
   Repository: https://github.com/MindLab-Research/dsh-generative-ui
   Contributed: the live-compiled TSX channel, the side canvas surface, and the
   "card reports its own failure back to the model" loop.

Claude artifact taxonomy (inline widgets, published pages, Slides, Design,
Docs, downloadable files) is modelled on Anthropic's published behaviour as
described by the user; this project is not affiliated with Anthropic.

The `cookbook/` directory is the user's Claude-authored visualization cookbook
(164 recipes, 9 recipe packs, 18 guide chapters, 7 Python scripts and the
standalone visual examples), included at the user's direction as the plugin's
source library. It is not an Anthropic product and carries no separate licence
file; the repository's MIT licence applies to the plugin code, while the
cookbook material remains the user's.

